Jenkins is an open-source automation server used to automate software development tasks such as building, testing, and deploying applications.
It is widely used to implement Continuous Integration (CI) and Continuous Delivery/Deployment (CD).
Jenkins supports integration with Git, GitHub, Docker, Kubernetes, Maven, Gradle, Ansible, Terraform, and cloud platforms.
Pipelines allow you to define the entire CI/CD workflow as code using a Jenkinsfile.
Jenkins supports Freestyle Projects for simple jobs and Pipeline Projects for more advanced automation.
It has a master (controller) and agent architecture, allowing builds to run on multiple machines.
Jenkins has a large plugin ecosystem with thousands of plugins to extend its functionality.
It can automatically trigger builds when code is pushed to a Git repository using webhooks or polling.
